    "content" : "The frequency of musculoskeletal pain regardless of localization was 48%. The analysis of the localization of pain on the body, we recognize that dominate acute in 15% and chronic pain in both shoulders in 22%. Acute pain in the right shoulder has a frequency of 19% and left only 1% (children are right-handed). Acute and chronic pain in the neck has the same prevalence, but which is high for this age, or 17%. Alarmingly high frequency also had presence of chronic back pain–16%, and chronic pain in the chest–12% (Table 2)."
